    "description": "Conjecture: Let f:X\u2192S be a semistable family of smooth projective varieties over a number field with generic fiber of fixed dimension d, and for each good prime p let D_p be the persistence diagram obtained from the filtered weight-monodromy complex of the mod-p nearby-cycles action on \u00e9tale cohomology. Then the collection {D_p}_p for a density-1 set of good primes determines the semisimplified geometric monodromy representation up to finite ambiguity. Test: Compute D_p for explicit non-isomorphic families with known monodromy (e.g. degenerating curves, K3 families, Calabi-Yau pencils) and check whether equal primewise persistence signatures force identical semisimplified monodromy; a counterexample refutes the conjecture. Impact: Would create a new arithmetic-topological observable for detecting hidden degeneration structure, linking persistent homology, \u00e9tale cohomology, and arithmetic geometry in a computable way.",
